# Frontend UI state (no magic values)

Apply on presentation/UI (`resources/ts/**/*.{ts,tsx}`). Do **not** rewrite existing pages into stores unless the user asks.

## Where logic lives

| Concern | Place |
|---|---|
| Auth session | Provider / context — login/logout/refresh only |
| Messages, lists, streaming | Store (Zustand or equivalent) — **no JSX, no fetch** |
| HTTP / SSE | Infrastructure + use cases — not in components |
| View composition | `*-view` wires store + presentational children |
| Pure UI | shell / list / item / composer — props in, callbacks out |

- Custom hooks: reusable **view** glue only (auto-scroll). Do not hide API calls in hooks.
- Do not add `useMemo` / `useCallback` by default.

Inertia pages may keep using `usePage()` / `router` for first-party form visits. New client API/SSE still goes through infrastructure + use cases.

## No magic status strings in JSX

- Status = const map / enum (`Status.Idle | Streaming | Error`), never a free `string`.
- Export **named selectors** (`selectIsStreaming`, `selectCanSend`).
- Views pass **boolean props**. Presentational components must not compare raw status.

```tsx
// ❌ disabled={status === "streaming"}
// ✅ <Composer canSend={canSend} isStreaming={isStreaming} />
```

## Store rules

- Store = state + behavior. No React components, no JSX, no `fetch`.
- Actions call use cases from the DI container (inject deps in tests).
- Select narrowly. Do not duplicate high-frequency state in Context.
- Always generic the store (`create<State>()`). Export a named `*State` type.
- `catch (error: unknown)` then narrow. No `any`.

## Components

- Presentational: data + named booleans + callbacks.
- Lists: stable `id` keys. Streaming hint via `isStreaming` prop, not a status literal.
- Abort in-flight streams on unmount via store `abort` or effect cleanup.

## Forbidden

- Inline `status === "…"` (or other magic strings) in JSX / presentational props
- One file owning layout + stream + markdown + sidebar
- Context for high-frequency message updates
- Coupling UI to backend tool names beyond displaying events
